  "id": "Compound::DB00920 - Gene::5151",
  "verbalization": "Ketotifen is shown to bind to Pde7b and Pde4c, both of which are involved in 3',5'-cyclic-amp phosphodiesterase activity, and this activity is associated with Pde8a. The evidence suggests that Ketotifen may influence Pde8a through a shared pathway involving the regulation of cyclic AMP degradation. The scores from the three paths indicate a consistent interaction between Ketotifen and Pde8a, with the strongest evidence pointing to Pde7b and Pde4c as potential intermediaries. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of phosphodiesterase activity, which could modulate intracellular cyclic AMP levels. The integration of these pathways supports a plausible mechanism by which Ketotifen may interact with Pde8a, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the role of Pde8a in this process.",
